      "value": "q0_pay_when_roi_clear",
      "rationale": "As a busy parent juggling multiple responsibilities, I'd need to see clear value in reducing my calendar fragmentation stress before committing to a subscription. The free tier lets me test whether it actually solves my WeChat-and-email chaos.",
      "confidence": 0.88
    },
    {
      "questionId": "q1",
      "value": "q1_plus_after_sustained_use",
      "rationale": "The core features I need (shared calendar, digest, handoffs) are in Plus, not Pro. Email parsing is nice-to-have but not essential. I'd upgrade to Plus once I'm confident the app becomes my household's single source of truth.",
      "confidence": 0.82
    },
    {
      "questionId": "q2",
      "value": "q2_monthly_cancel_anytime",
      "rationale": "I prefer flexibility with family apps—if our household routine changes or the app doesn't stick, I want to cancel without penalty. Annual prepay feels risky for a new product I haven't fully integrated yet.",
      "confidence": 0.85
    },
    {
      "questionId": "q3",
      "value": "q3_one_dollar_try_cancel",
      "rationale": "A $1 first month is low-friction enough to justify trying Plus features (digest, handoffs, 6 members) without guilt. If it doesn't meaningfully reduce my stress or missed deadlines within 30 days, I'll cancel.",
      "confidence": 0.86
    },
    {
      "questionId": "q4",
      "value": "q4_compare_pay_if_wins",
      "rationale": "I'm pragmatic about tools. If a friend recommends a paid organizer, I'll compare it to free options and FocusLoop, but I'll only pay if one clearly outperforms the others at solving my family's coordination pain.",
      "confidence": 0.84
    },
    {
      "questionId": "q5",
      "value": "q5_ads_pay_if_plus_useful",
      "rationale": "Ads on a free family app are mildly annoying but tolerable. I'd pay for Plus primarily because of the digest and handoffs, not to remove ads. Ad-free alone wouldn't justify the cost.",
      "confidence": 0.83
    },
    {
      "questionId": "q6",
      "value": "q6_fair_if_use_justifies",
      "rationale": "At $6.99/month, Plus is reasonable for a tool that could save me hours of weekly coordination stress. But only if daily use proves it's truly replacing my scattered channels. Otherwise it's just another subscription.",
      "confidence": 0.87
    },
    {
      "questionId": "overall_interest",
      "value": 4,
      "rationale": "The product directly addresses my biggest household pain point—fragmented communication across WeChat, email, and paper. The weekly digest and lightweight handoffs appeal to my need for calm visibility. Not a 5 because I need to validate it actually works in practice.",
      "confidence": 0.85
    },
